txtar/blank.txt "$\nBlank line at start and end.\n$\n"
  D "P(p<$\nBlank line at start and end.\n$>)"
txtar/code.txt "Text.\n\n\tA tab-indented\n\t(no, not eight-space indented)\n\tcode block and haiku.\n\nMore text.\n\n\tOne space\n\t is\n\t  enough\n\t   to\n\t    start\n\t     a\n\t      block.\n\nMore text.\n\n\t    Blocks\n\t  can\n\n\thave\n\t  blank\n\t    lines.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)C(A tab-indented\n(no, not eight-space indented)\ncode block and haiku.\n)P(p<More text.>)C(One space\n is\n  enough\n   to\n    start\n     a\n      block.\n)P(p<More text.>)C(    Blocks\n  can\n\nhave\n  blank\n    lines.\n)"
txtar/code2.txt "Text.\n\n\tA tab-indented\n\t(no, not eight-space indented)\n\tcode block and haiku.\n\nMore text.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)C(A tab-indented\n(no, not eight-space indented)\ncode block and haiku.\n)P(p<More text.>)"
txtar/code3.txt "Text.\n\n\t$\n\tA tab-indented\n\t(surrounded by more blank lines)\n\tcode block and haiku.\n\t$\n\nMore text.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)C($\nA tab-indented\n(surrounded by more blank lines)\ncode block and haiku.\n$\n)P(p<More text.>)"
txtar/code4.txt "To test, run this command:\n\n\tgo test -more\n\nOr, to test specific things, run this command:\n\n\tgo test -more \\\n\t  -pkg first/package \\\n\t  -pkg second/package \\\n\t  -pkg third/package\n\nHappy testing!\n"
  D "P(p<To test, run this command:>)C(go test -more\n)P(p<Or, to test specific things, run this command:>)C(go test -more \\\n  -pkg first/package \\\n  -pkg second/package \\\n  -pkg third/package\n)P(p<Happy testing!>)"
txtar/code5.txt "L1\nL2\nL3\nL4\nL5\n  - L6 {\n    L7\n    }\n\nL8\n"
  D "P(p<L1\nL2\nL3\nL4\nL5>)L(false,false,false,false #:P(p<L6 {\nL7\n}>))P(p<L8>)"
txtar/code6.txt "Run this program:\n\n\tfunc main() {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"hello, world\")\n\t}\n\nOr this:\n\n\tgo func() {\n\t\tfmt.Println(\"hello, world\")\n\t}()\n"
  D "P(p<Run this program:>)C(func main() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"hello, world\")\n}\n)P(p<Or this:>)C(go func() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"hello, world\")\n}()\n)"
txtar/crash1.txt "[]\n\n[]: http://\n"
  D "P(a<false,http://;>)[|http://|true]"
txtar/doclink.txt "In this package, see [Doc] and [Parser.Parse].\nThere is no [Undef] or [Undef.Method].\nSee also the [comment] package,\nespecially [comment.Doc] and [comment.Parser.Parse].\n"
  D "P(p<In this package, see [Doc] and [Parser.Parse].\nThere is no [Undef] or [Undef.Method].\nSee also the [comment] package,\nespecially [comment.Doc] and [comment.Parser.Parse].>)"
txtar/doclink2.txt "We use [io.Reader] a lot, and also a few map[io.Reader]string.\n\nNever [io.Reader]int or Slice[io.Reader] though.\n"
  D "P(p<We use >d<io,,Reader;p<io.Reader>>p< a lot, and also a few map[io.Reader]string.>)P(p<Never [io.Reader]int or Slice[io.Reader] though.>)"
txtar/doclink3.txt "[encoding/json.Marshal] is a doc link.\n\n[rot13.Marshal] is not.\n"
  D "P(d<encoding/json,,Marshal;p<encoding/json.Marshal>>p< is a doc link.>)P(p<[rot13.Marshal] is not.>)"
txtar/doclink4.txt "[io] at start of comment.\n[io] at start of line.\nAt end of line: [io]\nAt end of comment: [io]\n"
  D "P(d<io,,;p<io>>p< at start of comment.\n>d<io,,;p<io>>p< at start of line.\nAt end of line: >d<io,,;p<io>>p<\nAt end of comment: >d<io,,;p<io>>)"
txtar/doclink5.txt "[encoding/json.Marshal] is a doc link.\n"
  D "P(d<encoding/json,,Marshal;p<encoding/json.Marshal>>p< is a doc link.>)"
txtar/doclink6.txt "[encoding/json.Marshal] is a doc link, and so is [rsc.io/quote.NonExist].\n"
  D "P(d<encoding/json,,Marshal;p<encoding/json.Marshal>>p< is a doc link, and so is >d<rsc.io/quote,,NonExist;p<rsc.io/quote.NonExist>>p<.>)"
txtar/doclink7.txt "You see more [*bytes.Buffer] than [bytes.Buffer].\n"
  D "P(p<You see more >d<bytes,,Buffer;p<*bytes.Buffer>>p< than >d<bytes,,Buffer;p<bytes.Buffer>>p<.>)"
txtar/escape.txt "What the ~!@#$%^&*()_+-=`{}|[]\\:\";',./<>?\n\n+ Line\n\n- Line\n\n* Line\n\n999. Line\n\n## Line\n"
  D "P(p<What the ~!@#$%^&*()_+-=`{}|[]\\:\";',./<>?>)P(p<+ Line>)P(p<- Line>)P(p<* Line>)P(p<999. Line>)P(p<## Line>)"
txtar/head.txt "Some text.\n\n# An Old Heading\n\nNot An Old Heading.\n\nAnd some text.\n\n# A New Heading.\n\nAnd some more text.\n\n# Not a heading,\nbecause text follows it.\n\nBecause text precedes it,\n# not a heading.\n\n## Not a heading either.\n"
  D "P(p<Some text.>)H(p<An Old Heading>)P(p<Not An Old Heading.>)P(p<And some text.>)H(p<A New Heading.>)P(p<And some more text.>)P(p<# Not a heading,\nbecause text follows it.>)P(p<Because text precedes it,\n# not a heading.>)P(p<## Not a heading either.>)"
txtar/head2.txt "✦\n\nAlmost a+heading\n\n✦\n\nDon't be a heading\n\n✦\n\n# A.b is a heading\n\n✦\n\nA. b is not a heading\n\n✦\n"
  D "P(p<✦>)P(p<Almost a+heading>)P(p<✦>)P(p<Don't be a heading>)P(p<✦>)H(p<A.b is a heading>)P(p<✦>)P(p<A. b is not a heading>)P(p<✦>)"
txtar/head3.txt "# Heading\n"
  D "H(p<Heading>)"
txtar/hello.txt "Hello,\nworld\n\nThis is\na test.\n"
  D "P(p<Hello,\nworld>)P(p<This is\na test.>)"
txtar/link.txt "The Go home page is https://go.dev/.\nIt used to be https://golang.org.\n"
  D "P(p<The Go home page is >a<true,https://go.dev/;p<https://go.dev/>>p<.\nIt used to be >a<true,https://golang.org;p<https://golang.org>>p<.>)"
txtar/link2.txt "The Go home page is https://go.dev/.\nIt used to be https://golang.org.\nhttps:// is not a link.\nNor is https://\nhttps://☺ is not a link.\nhttps://:80 is not a link.\n"
  D "P(p<The Go home page is >a<true,https://go.dev/;p<https://go.dev/>>p<.\nIt used to be >a<true,https://golang.org;p<https://golang.org>>p<.\nhttps:// is not a link.\nNor is https://\nhttps://☺ is not a link.\nhttps://:80 is not a link.>)"
txtar/link3.txt "Doc text.\n\n[Go home page]: https://go.dev\n"
  D "P(p<Doc text.>)[Go home page|https://go.dev|false]"
txtar/link4.txt "These are not links.\n\n[x\n\n[x]:\n\n[x]:https://go.dev\n\n[x]https://go.dev\n\n[x]: surprise://go.dev\n\n[x]: surprise!\n\nBut this is, with a tab (although it's unused).\n\n[z]: https://go.dev\n"
  D "P(p<These are not links.>)P(p<[x>)P(p<[x]:>)P(p<[x]:>a<true,https://go.dev;p<https://go.dev>>)P(p<[x]>a<true,https://go.dev;p<https://go.dev>>)P(p<[x]: surprise://go.dev>)P(p<[x]: surprise!>)P(p<But this is, with a tab (although it's unused).>)[z|https://go.dev|false]"
txtar/link5.txt "See the [Go home page] and the [pkg\nsite].\n\nThey're really great!\n\n[Go home page]: https://go.dev/\n[pkg site]: https://pkg.go.dev\n\n[Go home page]: https://duplicate.ignored\n"
  D "P(p<See the >a<false,https://go.dev/;p<Go home page>>p< and the >a<false,https://pkg.go.dev;p<pkg\nsite>>p<.>)P(p<They're really great!>)[Go home page|https://go.dev/|true][pkg site|https://pkg.go.dev|true][Go home page|https://duplicate.ignored|false]"
txtar/link6.txt "URLs with punctuation are hard.\nWe don't want to consume the end-of-sentence punctuation.\n\nFor example, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Adams_(miniseries).\nAnd https://example.com/[foo]/bar{.\nAnd https://example.com/(foo)/bar!\nAnd https://example.com/{foo}/bar{.\nAnd https://example.com/)baz{foo}.\n\n[And https://example.com/].\n"
  D "P(p<URLs with punctuation are hard.\nWe don't want to consume the end-of-sentence punctuation.>)P(p<For example, >a<true,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Adams_(miniseries);p<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Adams_(miniseries)>>p<.\nAnd >a<true,https://example.com/[foo]/bar;p<https://example.com/[foo]/bar>>p<{.\nAnd >a<true,https://example.com/(foo)/bar;p<https://example.com/(foo)/bar>>p<!\nAnd >a<true,https://example.com/{foo}/bar;p<https://example.com/{foo}/bar>>p<{.\nAnd >a<true,https://example.com/;p<https://example.com/>>p<)baz{foo}.>)P(p<[And >a<true,https://example.com/;p<https://example.com/>>p<].>)"
txtar/link7.txt "[math] is a package but this is not a doc link.\n\n[io] is a doc link.\n\n[math]: https://example.com\n"
  D "P(a<false,https://example.com;p<math>>p< is a package but this is not a doc link.>)P(d<io,,;p<io>>p< is a doc link.>)[math|https://example.com|true]"
txtar/linklist.txt "Did you know?\n\n  - [encoding/json.Marshal] is a doc link. So is [encoding/json.Unmarshal].\n"
  D "P(p<Did you know?>)L(true,false,true,false #:P(d<encoding/json,,Marshal;p<encoding/json.Marshal>>p< is a doc link. So is >d<encoding/json,,Unmarshal;p<encoding/json.Unmarshal>>p<.>))"
txtar/linklist2.txt "Did you know?\n\n  - [testing.T] is one doc link.\n\n  - So is [testing.M].\n\n  - So is [testing.B].\n    This is the same list paragraph.\n\n    There is [testing.PB] in this list item, too!\n"
  D "P(p<Did you know?>)L(true,true,true,true #:P(d<testing,,T;p<testing.T>>p< is one doc link.>) #:P(p<So is >d<testing,,M;p<testing.M>>p<.>) #:P(p<So is >d<testing,,B;p<testing.B>>p<.\nThis is the same list paragraph.>)P(p<There is >d<testing,,PB;p<testing.PB>>p< in this list item, too!>))"
txtar/linklist3.txt "Cool things:\n\n  - Foo\n  - [Go]\n  - Bar\n\n[Go]: https://go.dev/\n"
  D "P(p<Cool things:>)L(true,false,true,false #:P(p<Foo>) #:P(a<false,https://go.dev/;p<Go>>) #:P(p<Bar>))[Go|https://go.dev/|true]"
txtar/linklist4.txt "Cool things:\n\n  - Foo\n\n  - [Go] is great\n\n  - Bar\n\n[Go]: https://go.dev/\n"
  D "P(p<Cool things:>)L(true,true,true,true #:P(p<Foo>) #:P(a<false,https://go.dev/;p<Go>>p< is great>) #:P(p<Bar>))[Go|https://go.dev/|true]"
txtar/list.txt "Text.\n- Not a list.\n  - Here is the list.\n  - Using multiple bullets.\n  - Indentation does not matter.\n  - Lots of bullets.\n\nMore text.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.\n- Not a list.>)L(false,false,false,false #:P(p<Here is the list.>) #:P(p<Using multiple bullets.>) #:P(p<Indentation does not matter.>) #:P(p<Lots of bullets.>))P(p<More text.>)"
txtar/list10.txt " 1. This list\n 2. Starts the comment\n 3. And also has a blank line before it.\n\nAll of which is a little weird.\n"
  D "L(false,false,false,false #1:P(p<This list>) #2:P(p<Starts the comment>) #3:P(p<And also has a blank line before it.>))P(p<All of which is a little weird.>)"
txtar/list2.txt "Text.\n 1. Uno\n 2. Dos\n 3. Tres\n 5. Cinco\n 7. Siete\n 11. Once\n 12. Doce\n 13. Trece.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)L(false,false,false,false #1:P(p<Uno>) #2:P(p<Dos>) #3:P(p<Tres>) #5:P(p<Cinco>) #7:P(p<Siete>) #11:P(p<Once>) #12:P(p<Doce>) #13:P(p<Trece.>))"
txtar/list3.txt "Text.\n\n 1. Uno\n 1. Dos\n 1. Tres\n 1. Quatro\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)L(true,false,true,false #1:P(p<Uno>) #1:P(p<Dos>) #1:P(p<Tres>) #1:P(p<Quatro>))"
txtar/list4.txt "Text.\n 1. List\n\n2. Not indented, not a list.\n 3. Another list.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)L(false,false,false,false #1:P(p<List>))P(p<2. Not indented, not a list.>)L(false,false,false,false #3:P(p<Another list.>))"
txtar/list5.txt "Text.\n\n 1. One\n 999999999999999999999. Big\n 1000000000000000000000. Bigger\n 1000000000000000000001. Biggest\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)L(true,false,true,false #1:P(p<One>) #999999999999999999999:P(p<Big>) #1000000000000000000000:P(p<Bigger>) #1000000000000000000001:P(p<Biggest>))"
txtar/list6.txt "Text.\n  - List immediately after.\n  - Another.\n\nMore text.\n\n  - List after blank line.\n  - Another.\n\nEven more text.\n\n  - List immediately after.\n\n  - Blank line between items.\n\nYet more text.\n\n  - Another list after blank line.\n\n  - Blank line between items.\n\nStill more text.\n\n  - One list item.\n\n    Multiple paragraphs.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)L(false,false,false,false #:P(p<List immediately after.>) #:P(p<Another.>))P(p<More text.>)L(true,false,true,false #:P(p<List after blank line.>) #:P(p<Another.>))P(p<Even more text.>)L(false,true,true,true #:P(p<List immediately after.>) #:P(p<Blank line between items.>))P(p<Yet more text.>)L(true,true,true,true #:P(p<Another list after blank line.>) #:P(p<Blank line between items.>))P(p<Still more text.>)L(false,true,true,true #:P(p<One list item.>)P(p<Multiple paragraphs.>))"
txtar/list7.txt "Almost list markers (but not quite):\n\n\t-\n\n❦\n\n  - $\n\n❦\n\n  - $\n\n❦\n\n\t$\n\t $\n\n❦\n\n\t1! List.\n\n❦\n"
  D "P(p<Almost list markers (but not quite):>)C(-\n)P(p<❦>)L(true,false,true,false #:P(p<$>))P(p<❦>)L(true,false,true,false #:P(p<$>))P(p<❦>)C($\n $\n)P(p<❦>)C(1! List.\n)P(p<❦>)"
txtar/list8.txt "Loose lists.\n\n  - A\n\n    B\n\n  - C\n    D\n\n  - E\n\n  - F\n"
  D "P(p<Loose lists.>)L(false,true,true,true #:P(p<A>)P(p<B>) #:P(p<C\nD>) #:P(p<E>) #:P(p<F>))"
txtar/list9.txt "Text.\n\n1. Not a list\n2. because it is\n3. unindented.\n\n 4. This one\n    is a list\n    because of the indented text.\n 5. More wrapped\n    items.\n 6. And unwrapped.\n\n7. The blank line stops the heuristic.\n"
  D "P(p<Text.>)P(p<1. Not a list\n2. because it is\n3. unindented.>)L(true,false,true,false #4:P(p<This one\nis a list\nbecause of the indented text.>) #5:P(p<More wrapped\nitems.>) #6:P(p<And unwrapped.>))P(p<7. The blank line stops the heuristic.>)"
txtar/para.txt "Hello, world.\nThis is a paragraph.\n"
  D "P(p<Hello, world.\nThis is a paragraph.>)"
txtar/quote.txt "Doubled single quotes like “ and ” turn into Unicode double quotes,\nbut single quotes ` and ' do not.\nMisplaced markdown fences ``` do not either.\n"
  D "P(p<Doubled single quotes like “ and ” turn into Unicode double quotes,\nbut single quotes ` and ' do not.\nMisplaced markdown fences ``` do not either.>)"
txtar/text.txt "Hello, world\n\n\tCode block here.\n\nMore text.\nTight list\n  - one\n  - two\n  - three\n\nLoose list\n\n  - one\n\n  - two\n\n  - three\n\n# Heading\n\nMore text.\n"
  D "P(p<Hello, world>)C(Code block here.\n)P(p<More text.\nTight list>)L(false,false,false,false #:P(p<one>) #:P(p<two>) #:P(p<three>))P(p<Loose list>)L(false,true,true,true #:P(p<one>) #:P(p<two>) #:P(p<three>))H(p<Heading>)P(p<More text.>)"
txtar/text2.txt "Package gob manages streams of gobs - binary values exchanged between an\nEncoder (transmitter) and a Decoder (receiver). A typical use is\ntransporting arguments and results of remote procedure calls (RPCs) such as\nthose provided by package \"net/rpc\".\n\nThe implementation compiles a custom codec for each data type in the stream\nand is most efficient when a single Encoder is used to transmit a stream of\nvalues, amortizing the cost of compilation.\n"
  D "P(p<Package gob manages streams of gobs - binary values exchanged between an\nEncoder (transmitter) and a Decoder (receiver). A typical use is\ntransporting arguments and results of remote procedure calls (RPCs) such as\nthose provided by package \"net/rpc\".>)P(p<The implementation compiles a custom codec for each data type in the stream\nand is most efficient when a single Encoder is used to transmit a stream of\nvalues, amortizing the cost of compilation.>)"
