strings/strings.go#34 "FieldsFunc splits the string s at each run of Unicode code points c satisfying f(c)\nand returns an array of slices of s. If all code points in s satisfy f(c) or the\nstring is empty, an empty slice is returned. Every element of the returned slice is\nnon-empty. Unlike [Split], leading and trailing runs of code points satisfying f(c)\nare discarded.\n\nFieldsFunc makes no guarantees about the order in which it calls f(c)\nand assumes that f always returns the same value for a given c.\n"
  D "P(p<FieldsFunc splits the string s at each run of Unicode code points c satisfying f(c)\nand returns an array of slices of s. If all code points in s satisfy f(c) or the\nstring is empty, an empty slice is returned. Every element of the returned slice is\nnon-empty. Unlike [Split], leading and trailing runs of code points satisfying f(c)\nare discarded.>)P(p<FieldsFunc makes no guarantees about the order in which it calls f(c)\nand assumes that f always returns the same value for a given c.>)"
