go/doc/comment/parse.go#35 "ImportPath, Recv, and Name identify the Go package or symbol\nthat is the link target. The potential combinations of\nnon-empty fields are:\n  - ImportPath: a link to another package\n  - ImportPath, Name: a link to a const, func, type, or var in another package\n  - ImportPath, Recv, Name: a link to a method in another package\n  - Name: a link to a const, func, type, or var in this package\n  - Recv, Name: a link to a method in this package\n"
  D "P(p<ImportPath, Recv, and Name identify the Go package or symbol\nthat is the link target. The potential combinations of\nnon-empty fields are:>)L(false,false,false,false #:P(p<ImportPath: a link to another package>) #:P(p<ImportPath, Name: a link to a const, func, type, or var in another package>) #:P(p<ImportPath, Recv, Name: a link to a method in another package>) #:P(p<Name: a link to a const, func, type, or var in this package>) #:P(p<Recv, Name: a link to a method in this package>))"
