  D "P(p<Give LookupPackage a chance.>)"
go/doc/comment/parse.go#47 "DefaultLookupPackage is the default package lookup\nfunction, used when [Parser.LookupPackage] is nil.\nIt recognizes names of the packages from the standard\nlibrary with single-element import paths, such as math,\nwhich would otherwise be impossible to name.\n\nNote that the go/doc package provides a more sophisticated\nlookup based on the imports used in the current package.\n"
  D "P(p<DefaultLookupPackage is the default package lookup\nfunction, used when [Parser.LookupPackage] is nil.\nIt recognizes names of the packages from the standard\nlibrary with single-element import paths, such as math,\nwhich would otherwise be impossible to name.>)P(p<Note that the go/doc package provides a more sophisticated\nlookup based on the imports used in the current package.>)"
