go/doc/comment/print.go#1 "A Printer is a doc comment printer.\nThe fields in the struct can be filled in before calling\nany of the printing methods\nin order to customize the details of the printing process.\n"
  D "P(p<A Printer is a doc comment printer.\nThe fields in the struct can be filled in before calling\nany of the printing methods\nin order to customize the details of the printing process.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#2 "HeadingLevel is the nesting level used for\nHTML and Markdown headings.\nIf HeadingLevel is zero, it defaults to level 3,\nmeaning to use <h3> and ###.\n"
  D "P(p<HeadingLevel is the nesting level used for\nHTML and Markdown headings.\nIf HeadingLevel is zero, it defaults to level 3,\nmeaning to use <h3> and ###.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#3 "HeadingID is a function that computes the heading ID\n(anchor tag) to use for the heading h when generating\nHTML and Markdown. If HeadingID returns an empty string,\nthen the heading ID is omitted.\nIf HeadingID is nil, h.DefaultID is used.\n"
  D "P(p<HeadingID is a function that computes the heading ID\n(anchor tag) to use for the heading h when generating\nHTML and Markdown. If HeadingID returns an empty string,\nthen the heading ID is omitted.\nIf HeadingID is nil, h.DefaultID is used.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#4 "DocLinkURL is a function that computes the URL for the given DocLink.\nIf DocLinkURL is nil, then link.DefaultURL(p.DocLinkBaseURL) is used.\n"
  D "P(p<DocLinkURL is a function that computes the URL for the given DocLink.\nIf DocLinkURL is nil, then link.DefaultURL(p.DocLinkBaseURL) is used.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#5 "DocLinkBaseURL is used when DocLinkURL is nil,\npassed to [DocLink.DefaultURL] to construct a DocLink's URL.\nSee that method's documentation for details.\n"
  D "P(p<DocLinkBaseURL is used when DocLinkURL is nil,\npassed to [DocLink.DefaultURL] to construct a DocLink's URL.\nSee that method's documentation for details.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#6 "TextPrefix is a prefix to print at the start of every line\nwhen generating text output using the Text method.\n"
  D "P(p<TextPrefix is a prefix to print at the start of every line\nwhen generating text output using the Text method.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#7 "TextCodePrefix is the prefix to print at the start of each\npreformatted (code block) line when generating text output,\ninstead of (not in addition to) TextPrefix.\nIf TextCodePrefix is the empty string, it defaults to TextPrefix+\"\\t\".\n"
  D "P(p<TextCodePrefix is the prefix to print at the start of each\npreformatted (code block) line when generating text output,\ninstead of (not in addition to) TextPrefix.\nIf TextCodePrefix is the empty string, it defaults to TextPrefix+\"\\t\".>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#8 "TextWidth is the maximum width text line to generate,\nmeasured in Unicode code points,\nexcluding TextPrefix and the newline character.\nIf TextWidth is zero, it defaults to 80 minus the number of code points in TextPrefix.\nIf TextWidth is negative, there is no limit.\n"
  D "P(p<TextWidth is the maximum width text line to generate,\nmeasured in Unicode code points,\nexcluding TextPrefix and the newline character.\nIf TextWidth is zero, it defaults to 80 minus the number of code points in TextPrefix.\nIf TextWidth is negative, there is no limit.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#9 "DefaultURL constructs and returns the documentation URL for l,\nusing baseURL as a prefix for links to other packages.\n\nThe possible forms returned by DefaultURL are:\n  - baseURL/ImportPath, for a link to another package\n  - baseURL/ImportPath#Name, for a link to a const, func, type, or var in another package\n  - baseURL/ImportPath#Recv.Name, for a link to a method in another package\n  - #Name, for a link to a const, func, type, or var in this package\n  - #Recv.Name, for a link to a method in this package\n\nIf baseURL ends in a trailing slash, then DefaultURL inserts\na slash between ImportPath and # in the anchored forms.\nFor example, here are some baseURL values and URLs they can generate:\n\n\t\"/pkg/\" → \"/pkg/math/#Sqrt\"\n\t\"/pkg\"  → \"/pkg/math#Sqrt\"\n\t\"/\"     → \"/math/#Sqrt\"\n\t\"\"      → \"/math#Sqrt\"\n"
  D "P(p<DefaultURL constructs and returns the documentation URL for l,\nusing baseURL as a prefix for links to other packages.>)P(p<The possible forms returned by DefaultURL are:>)L(false,false,false,false #:P(p<baseURL/ImportPath, for a link to another package>) #:P(p<baseURL/ImportPath#Name, for a link to a const, func, type, or var in another package>) #:P(p<baseURL/ImportPath#Recv.Name, for a link to a method in another package>) #:P(p<#Name, for a link to a const, func, type, or var in this package>) #:P(p<#Recv.Name, for a link to a method in this package>))P(p<If baseURL ends in a trailing slash, then DefaultURL inserts\na slash between ImportPath and # in the anchored forms.\nFor example, here are some baseURL values and URLs they can generate:>)C(\"/pkg/\" → \"/pkg/math/#Sqrt\"\n\"/pkg\"  → \"/pkg/math#Sqrt\"\n\"/\"     → \"/math/#Sqrt\"\n\"\"      → \"/math#Sqrt\"\n)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#10 "DefaultID returns the default anchor ID for the heading h.\n\nThe default anchor ID is constructed by converting every\nrune that is not alphanumeric ASCII to an underscore\nand then adding the prefix “hdr-”.\nFor example, if the heading text is “Go Doc Comments”,\nthe default ID is “hdr-Go_Doc_Comments”.\n"
  D "P(p<DefaultID returns the default anchor ID for the heading h.>)P(p<The default anchor ID is constructed by converting every\nrune that is not alphanumeric ASCII to an underscore\nand then adding the prefix “hdr-”.\nFor example, if the heading text is “Go Doc Comments”,\nthe default ID is “hdr-Go_Doc_Comments”.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#11 "Note: The “hdr-” prefix is important to avoid DOM clobbering attacks.\nSee https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/google/safehtml#Identifier.\n"
  D "P(p<Note: The “hdr-” prefix is important to avoid DOM clobbering attacks.\nSee >a<true,https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/google/safehtml#Identifier;p<https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/google/safehtml#Identifier>>p<.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#12 "Comment returns the standard Go formatting of the [Doc],\nwithout any comment markers.\n"
  D "P(p<Comment returns the standard Go formatting of the [Doc],\nwithout any comment markers.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#13 "Print one block containing all the link definitions that were used,\nand then a second block containing all the unused ones.\nThis makes it easy to clean up the unused ones: gofmt and\ndelete the final block. And it's a nice visual signal without\naffecting the way the comment formats for users.\n"
  D "P(p<Print one block containing all the link definitions that were used,\nand then a second block containing all the unused ones.\nThis makes it easy to clean up the unused ones: gofmt and\ndelete the final block. And it's a nice visual signal without\naffecting the way the comment formats for users.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#14 "blankBefore reports whether the block x requires a blank line before it.\nAll blocks do, except for Lists that return false from x.BlankBefore().\n"
  D "P(p<blankBefore reports whether the block x requires a blank line before it.\nAll blocks do, except for Lists that return false from x.BlankBefore().>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#15 "block prints the block x to out.\n"
  D "P(p<block prints the block x to out.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#16 "text prints the text sequence x to out.\n"
  D "P(p<text prints the text sequence x to out.>)"
go/doc/comment/print.go#17 "indent prints s to out, indenting with the indent string\nafter each newline in s.\n"
  D "P(p<indent prints s to out, indenting with the indent string\nafter each newline in s.>)"
