  D "P(p<See the reference implementation in gen_encoding_table.go.>)"
net/url/url.go#8 "QueryUnescape does the inverse transformation of [QueryEscape],\nconverting each 3-byte encoded substring of the form \"%AB\" into the\nhex-decoded byte 0xAB.\nIt returns an error if any % is not followed by two hexadecimal\ndigits.\n"
  D "P(p<QueryUnescape does the inverse transformation of [QueryEscape],\nconverting each 3-byte encoded substring of the form \"%AB\" into the\nhex-decoded byte 0xAB.\nIt returns an error if any % is not followed by two hexadecimal\ndigits.>)"
net/url/url.go#9 "PathUnescape does the inverse transformation of [PathEscape],\nconverting each 3-byte encoded substring of the form \"%AB\" into the\nhex-decoded byte 0xAB. It returns an error if any % is not followed\nby two hexadecimal digits.\n\nPathUnescape is identical to [QueryUnescape] except that it does not\nunescape '+' to ' ' (space).\n"
  D "P(p<PathUnescape does the inverse transformation of [PathEscape],\nconverting each 3-byte encoded substring of the form \"%AB\" into the\nhex-decoded byte 0xAB. It returns an error if any % is not followed\nby two hexadecimal digits.>)P(p<PathUnescape is identical to [QueryUnescape] except that it does not\nunescape '+' to ' ' (space).>)"
net/url/url.go#10 "unescape unescapes a string; the mode specifies\nwhich section of the URL string is being unescaped.\n"
  D "P(p<unescape unescapes a string; the mode specifies\nwhich section of the URL string is being unescaped.>)"
net/url/url.go#11 "Count %, check that they're well-formed.\n"
  D "P(p<Count %, check that they're well-formed.>)"
net/url/url.go#12 "Per https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986#page-21\nin the host component %-encoding can only be used\nfor non-ASCII bytes.\nBut https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6874#section-2\nintroduces %25 being allowed to escape a percent sign\nin IPv6 scoped-address literals. Yay.\n"
  D "P(p<Per >a<true,https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986#page-21;p<https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3986#page-21>>p<\nin the host component %-encoding can only be used\nfor non-ASCII bytes.\nBut >a<true,https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6874#section-2;p<https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6874#section-2>>p<\nintroduces %25 being allowed to escape a percent sign\nin IPv6 scoped-address literals. Yay.>)"
net/url/url.go#13 "RFC 6874 says basically \"anything goes\" for zone identifiers\nand that even non-ASCII can be redundantly escaped,\nbut it seems prudent to restrict %-escaped bytes here to those\nthat are valid host name bytes in their unescaped form.\nThat is, you can use escaping in the zone identifier but not\nto introduce bytes you couldn't just write directly.\nBut Windows puts spaces here! Yay.\n"
  D "P(p<RFC 6874 says basically \"anything goes\" for zone identifiers\nand that even non-ASCII can be redundantly escaped,\nbut it seems prudent to restrict %-escaped bytes here to those\nthat are valid host name bytes in their unescaped form.\nThat is, you can use escaping in the zone identifier but not\nto introduce bytes you couldn't just write directly.\nBut Windows puts spaces here! Yay.>)"
