net/url/url.go#95 "JoinPath returns a new [URL] with the provided path elements joined to\nany existing path and the resulting path cleaned of any ./ or ../ elements.\nAny sequences of multiple / characters will be reduced to a single /.\nPath elements must already be in escaped form, as produced by [PathEscape].\n"
  D "P(p<JoinPath returns a new [URL] with the provided path elements joined to\nany existing path and the resulting path cleaned of any ./ or ../ elements.\nAny sequences of multiple / characters will be reduced to a single /.\nPath elements must already be in escaped form, as produced by [PathEscape].>)"
net/url/url.go#96 "Return a relative path if u is relative,\nbut ensure that it contains no ../ elements.\n"
  D "P(p<Return a relative path if u is relative,\nbut ensure that it contains no ../ elements.>)"
net/url/url.go#97 "path.Join will remove any trailing slashes.\nPreserve at least one.\n"
  D "P(p<path.Join will remove any trailing slashes.\nPreserve at least one.>)"
net/url/url.go#98 "validUserinfo reports whether s is a valid userinfo string per RFC 3986\nSection 3.2.1:\n\n\tuserinfo    = *( unreserved / pct-encoded / sub-delims / \":\" )\n\tunreserved  = ALPHA / DIGIT / \"-\" / \".\" / \"_\" / \"~\"\n\tsub-delims  = \"!\" / \"$\" / \"&\" / \"'\" / \"(\" / \")\"\n\t              / \"*\" / \"+\" / \",\" / \";\" / \"=\"\n\nIt doesn't validate pct-encoded. The caller does that via func unescape.\n"
  D "P(p<validUserinfo reports whether s is a valid userinfo string per RFC 3986\nSection 3.2.1:>)C(userinfo    = *( unreserved / pct-encoded / sub-delims / \":\" )\nunreserved  = ALPHA / DIGIT / \"-\" / \".\" / \"_\" / \"~\"\nsub-delims  = \"!\" / \"$\" / \"&\" / \"'\" / \"(\" / \")\"\n              / \"*\" / \"+\" / \",\" / \";\" / \"=\"\n)P(p<It doesn't validate pct-encoded. The caller does that via func unescape.>)"
net/url/url.go#99 "`RFC 3986 section 3.2.1` does not allow '@' in userinfo.\nIt is a delimiter between userinfo and host.\nHowever, URLs are diverse, and in some cases,\nthe userinfo may contain an '@' character,\nfor example, in \"http://username:p@ssword@google.com\",\nthe string \"username:p@ssword\" should be treated as valid userinfo.\nRef:\n\n\thttps://go.dev/issue/3439\n\thttps://go.dev/issue/22655\n"
  D "P(p<`RFC 3986 section 3.2.1` does not allow '@' in userinfo.\nIt is a delimiter between userinfo and host.\nHowever, URLs are diverse, and in some cases,\nthe userinfo may contain an '@' character,\nfor example, in \">a<true,http://username:p@ssword@google.com;p<http://username:p@ssword@google.com>>p<\",\nthe string \"username:p@ssword\" should be treated as valid userinfo.\nRef:>)C(https://go.dev/issue/3439\nhttps://go.dev/issue/22655\n)"
net/url/url.go#100 "stringContainsCTLByte reports whether s contains any ASCII control character.\n"
  D "P(p<stringContainsCTLByte reports whether s contains any ASCII control character.>)"
net/url/url.go#101 "JoinPath returns a [URL] string with the provided path elements joined to\nthe existing path of base and the resulting path cleaned of any ./ or ../ elements.\nPath elements must already be in escaped form, as produced by [PathEscape].\n"
  D "P(p<JoinPath returns a [URL] string with the provided path elements joined to\nthe existing path of base and the resulting path cleaned of any ./ or ../ elements.\nPath elements must already be in escaped form, as produced by [PathEscape].>)"
net/url/url.go#102 "Clone creates a deep copy of the fields of the subject [URL].\n"
  D "P(p<Clone creates a deep copy of the fields of the subject [URL].>)"
